EndDate is set by base (`QCAlgorithm`) to `DateTime.Now.AddDays(-1)`; 

In the case of EndDate being -1 days from StartDate it doesn't cause any problems with History requests. I think this would only be an issue in the case of QB running as an Algorithm. 

In the `else` statement if we use EndDate it is possible for a user in UTC + 12 after 8am in NY (with default 9AM hour threshold) to fail the first `if` and still set the date to the current NY Day before the threshold has passed. I figure this way we cover the edge case and never make requests for data that is not available yet.

I just checked setting `EndDate` to newYorkTime, but it actually has a verification check that stops anything greater than yesterday being set :/

```
            if (end > DateTime.Now.Date.AddDays(-1))
            {
                end = DateTime.Now.Date.AddDays(-1);
            }
```

So we won't be able to change it to the current day.
